{#
  Base page skeleton for the DutchBay wizard frontend (#843, epic #788).

  Loads the vendored htmx runtime and the wizard stylesheet, then exposes a
  single ``content`` block that concrete pages (login, wizard) fill. Fragment
  templates (``_results.html.j2`` / ``_error.html.j2``) do NOT extend this file;
  they are returned raw for htmx to swap into ``#results``.

  Security: this project's Jinja2 environment is constructed with
  ``autoescape = True`` for the ``.html.j2`` suffix, so every interpolated value
  is HTML-escaped by default. Do not disable it for user-supplied fields.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{% block title %}DutchBay EPC Model{% endblock %}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/app.css" />
    <script src="/static/vendor/htmx.min.js" defer></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="site-header__inner">
        <span class="site-header__brand">DutchBay EPC Model</span>
        <span class="site-header__tagline">Wind project finance</span>
        {% block header_actions %}{% endblock %}
      </div>
    </header>
    <main class="site-main">
      {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="site-footer__inner">
        <span
          >Screening output only. Not a bankable connection study or investment
          advice.</span
        >
      </div>
    </footer>
    <script>
      // htmx swaps only 2xx/3xx responses by default. The wizard's validation /
      // engine-rejection errors come back as 400/422 (honest client-error status)
      // with the _error fragment as the body; opt those into the swap so the error
      // renders in #results instead of being silently discarded (#843). These are
      // expected client errors, not system errors, so clear isError to keep htmx
      // from logging them as failures.
      document.body.addEventListener("htmx:beforeSwap", function (event) {
        var status = event.detail.xhr.status;
        if (status === 400 || status === 422) {
          event.detail.shouldSwap = true;
          event.detail.isError = false;
        }
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
